            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Ideally both. A dehumidifier addresses the root cause by keeping relative humidity below 50%, which prevents new mold growth. An air purifier addresses the symptom by removing spores already circulating in the air. If you can only afford one and you have active visible mold, fix the moisture problem with a dehumidifier first — an air purifier alone won't stop mold from growing.",
