          <p>
            This is non-negotiable. True HEPA filters are independently certified to capture 99.97% of particles at 0.3 microns — the hardest size to trap. Mold spores at 2-10 microns are considerably larger and get caught even more reliably. Marketing terms like "HEPA-type," "HEPA-like," or "99% HEPA" describe filters that haven't met the certified standard and can let significantly more particles through. Always confirm "True HEPA" or "HEPA H13" in the specifications.
