              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying "HEPA-Type" Instead of True HEPA</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Marketing terms like "HEPA-type," "HEPA-like," or "99% HEPA" describe filters that have not met the independently certified HEPA standard, and can let meaningfully more particles through than the real thing. Always confirm the listing says "True HEPA" or references the H13 certification standard before buying — this single word is the difference between a purifier that works and one that doesn't.
